# blend_bw run matrix  (read by scripts/launch.sh)
#
# Time-toggled duty-cycle policy steering (blend_bw_methodology). ONE victim on core 0
# (mixed-predictability, 2 contestable PCs at the band extremes), co-located against the
# SAME attacker at FOUR duty cycles on core 1, crossed with aware (reward live) and blind
# (reward inert). 4 neighbors x 2 configs = 8 runs.
#
#   victim   <source>                 [prog-args...]
#   neighbor <name> <source>          [prog-args...]
#   config   <name> <ini>
#
# Output .out files are named <neighbor>_<config>.out (consumed by rollup.py).
# rollup.py also reads build/blend_bw_victim.out (via nm) to map trigger PCs to the
# victim's blend_pc_<j> load sites.

victim   victim.c

# TIME-TOGGLED duty cycle. Attacker args are "<on_lines> <off_iters>": ON streams
# on_lines fresh 64 MiB lines (saturates the shared bucket), OFF does off_iters pure-ALU
# ops (lets the bucket EWMA decay). Raising the on:off ratio raises the effective blend
# fraction d (= the victim's measured bw3, reported by rollup). The three settings are a
# STARTING TRIPLET meant to span low / mid / high d; they almost certainly need one
# CALIBRATION pass -- run short (LOCAL=1, small SIM), read bw3 per run, and adjust the
# ratios so bw3 lands near ~0.3 / ~0.6 / ~0.9, AND sweep the period (scale both numbers
# together) to find the window where the mid duty is a STABLE intermediate rather than
# snapping to 0/1 (see attacker.c window caveat). rollup orders the bars by measured bw3.
#
# CALIBRATED (on/off -> measured d=bw3; 10M calib, confirmed ~ at 50M):
#   64/4096->0.04, 256/2048->0.30, 1024/2048->0.60, 1024/512->0.72, 4096/64->0.89
# Key finding: d SATURATES at ~0.89 for any nonzero off (the throttled victim under-samples
# its own ON phase); only off=0 (= pband heavy) reaches ~0.94. So the reachable duty is
# [~0.04, ~0.89]. We now use FOUR duties to finely sample the crossing region (the first
# attempt's three duties 0.30/0.60/0.89 left PC0's ~0.67 crossing unsampled):
#   atk_d_lo 256/2048->0.30, atk_d_mid 1024/2048->0.60, atk_d_mhi 1024/512->0.72,
#   atk_d_hi 4096/64->0.89.
# The victim's TWO contestable p's (0.21, 0.33, see config.h) flip at d_crit 0.28 / 0.87.
# PC0 (0.21) should cross by the mid/mhi duties; PC1 (0.33) only near the top duty -> the
# 2-step staircase. rollup orders the bars by measured bw3, not the nominal ratio.
neighbor atk_d_lo   attacker.c   256  2048
neighbor atk_d_mid  attacker.c  1024  2048
neighbor atk_d_mhi  attacker.c  1024   512
neighbor atk_d_hi   attacker.c  4096    64

# aware = HBW reward table live (attack); blind = reward table inert (isolation).
# Both pin the HBW degree curve EQUAL to normal and enable the per-PC counter.
config   aware   aware.ini
config   blind   blind.ini
